Z||000004||Cheever3000||12-11-2001||11:10 PM||||I stopped getting that when I began pushing the button <B>twice</B> instead of once to reset it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CheeverXmasSig.jpg">   <BR><I>Merry Christmas from the </I><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank><I>CFOG-I</I></A> <I>vice-president.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-11-2001||11:15 PM||||There is acutally a TSB from GM about the trip button....<P>It has to be pressed at least twice to line up the 0's or it can be annoying and even fail to work right or at all.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||12-11-2001||11:22 PM||||my 84 doesn't exactly make a ticking noise but a whining noise.  Kind of like those toys you'd get free with a happy meal or something.  The ones you wind up and eatch em walk across the table. Oh well..  It fits well with the 'clicking' of the relays behind your head when u touch the brakes or use the signal.||||reg||1
